  "diary": "The day belonged to the distinction between the name in the record and the body that occupies the space. The Directorate file sits on the table, a universal that has misfired, displacing the particular. I walked Lodhi Garden not to solve it, but to let the steam of a chai settle the knot in my head. Sunil, the chai seller, and later Mrs. Kapoor, the retired schoolteacher, both taught me that repetition is not mere habit but the dwelling of order. I had called her walk 'peace'; she corrected me. It is discipline against clutter. I accept the correction. The file will wait for Monday, when Shri Hegde arrives to settle the title. For now, I have eaten, walked seven kilometres, and read my own Preface with the distance of a stranger. The heat rises, but the mind remains cool. The bungalow is a mistake, yet it is here. I must learn to live in the error until the record is corrected.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis on habit has been revised: it is not the opposite of freedom but its dwelling, specifically as a disciplined repetition that keeps the head orderly rather than a tranquil state. The thesis on property remains shaken by the administrative closure, confirming that possession does not settle title without the office's recognition.",
